WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:15.113
I could not believe it.

2
00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:18.833
Tufty had flown out through my skylight!

3
00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:23.986
"Tufty won't be able to find his way home!" Molly cried.

4
00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:29.889
"He doesn't have a bell like I do," said Caswell sadly.

5
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.938
"Even if someone finds him, they won't know he's my parrot," Molly went on.

6
00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:38.935
Her eyes filled with tears.

7
00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:44.307
"I'll never see Tufty again!"

8
00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:48.425
We ran into the living room and told my mom what had happened.

9
00:00:48.426 --> 00:00:50.067
My mom sat down.

10
00:00:50.068 --> 00:00:52.060
She looked worried.

11
00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:56.681
"Are you sure Tufty flew through the skylight?" she asked.

12
00:00:56.682 --> 00:01:02.087
"We looked all over my room," I said, "and he's not there."

13
00:01:02.088 --> 00:01:06.179
"Go find Mr. Calabria," my mom said.

14
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.923
"See if he'll help us look for Tufty."

15
00:01:09.924 --> 00:01:13.585
We found Mr. Calabria in his workshop.

16
00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:15.622
He smiled when he saw us.

17
00:01:15.623 --> 00:01:17.567
"Good news, everybody.

18
00:01:17.568 --> 00:01:21.493
You'll be able to turn on your air conditioners again tonight!"

19
00:01:21.494 --> 00:01:26.379
"We came to see you about something else," Molly explained.

20
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.463
"We need help finding my parrot."

21
00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:33.756
"He flew through my skylight," I explained.

22
00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:37.379
"Oh dear," said Mr. Calabria.

23
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.308
"Let's go see if we can spot him."

24
00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:43.734
Everyone except Molly went up to the roof.

25
00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:49.414
Her mom didn't want her to climb the narrow stairs with her boot.

26
00:01:49.415 --> 00:01:53.847
From the roof of our building, you can see all over the city.

27
00:01:53.848 --> 00:01:58.681
I could see the tops of apartment buildings and a big bridge.

28
00:01:58.682 --> 00:02:02.466
But I didn't see any sign of Tufty.

29
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:07.226
We all looked and listened for him.

30
00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:16.725
We heard car horns and subway trains, but this time they were real horns and real trains.

31
00:02:16.726 --> 00:02:20.290
Mr. Calabria peered down at the street.

32
00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:25.435
"A police car is stopping in front of our building!" he said.

33
00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:29.437
"I'd better go down and see what the police officers want."

34
00:02:29.438 --> 00:02:35.113
We followed Mr. Calabria downstairs.

35
00:02:35.114 --> 00:02:39.607
And you'll never believe what happened next!

36
00:02:39.608 --> 00:02:42.128
A policewoman stepped out of the car.

37
00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:45.010
She was holding a big box.

38
00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:48.625
"Do the O'Donnells live here?" she asked.

39
00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:53.256
"Yes," said Mr. Calabria. "Is something wrong?"

40
00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:55.315
The policewoman smiled.

41
00:02:55.316 --> 00:03:00.417
"I have something for them."

42
00:03:00.418 --> 00:03:04.032
I heard a sound from inside the box.

43
00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.162
"My number is 555...

44
00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:09.551
I never get it wrong!"

45
00:03:09.552 --> 00:03:15.155
"That's Tufty!" I cried. "He's singing Molly's telephone number!"

46
00:03:15.156 --> 00:03:20.288
"He's my parrot!" said Molly happily.

47
00:03:20.289 --> 00:03:24.331
"We found Tufty in the park," the policewoman explained.

48
00:03:24.332 --> 00:03:28.558
"We were able to trace the telephone number back to Molly's family."

49
00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:31.755
Molly was thrilled to see Tufty.

50
00:03:31.756 --> 00:03:36.192
After that the parrot spent all his time sitting on Molly's walking boot.

51
00:03:36.193 --> 00:03:38.564
He loved to peck at it.

52
00:03:38.565 --> 00:03:42.101
The rest of the summer went by really fast.

53
00:03:42.102 --> 00:03:46.625
We kept trying to teach Tufty to talk.

54
00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:50.543
But he just kept singing the telephone number song.

55
00:03:50.544 --> 00:03:55.165
Luckily, he never made any more loud noises.

56
00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:57.154
Oh, and guess what.

57
00:03:57.155 --> 00:04:03.230
As soon as our air conditioners started working again, the heat wave was over!

58
00:04:03.231 --> 00:04:07.050
"It's going to get cold tonight," my mom said.

59
00:04:07.051 --> 00:04:10.514
"We might even need to put on our sweaters."

60
00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:13.344
"Cool!" said Tate.

61
00:04:13.345 --> 00:04:19.368
That made everyone laugh.

62
00:04:19.369 --> 00:04:21.040
Molly grinned at me.

63
00:04:21.041 --> 00:04:23.372
"I'm glad the heat wave is over.

64
00:04:23.373 --> 00:04:25.940
But I'm also glad we had a heat wave.

65
00:04:25.941 --> 00:04:32.777
Otherwise, you would not have invented an air-conditioned movie theater in your room, Iggy."

66
00:04:32.778 --> 00:04:35.966
"Yeah," agreed Josh.

67
00:04:35.967 --> 00:04:40.386
"And it's a good thing you thought of showing The Magic Music Box.

68
00:04:40.387 --> 00:04:45.119
Otherwise, Tufty might have been lost forever!"

69
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:50.390
"Luckily, Tufty could sing his telephone number!" added Jenny.

70
00:04:50.391 --> 00:04:56.514
So, as usual, my incredible inventions had worked.

71
00:04:56.515 --> 00:05:04.854
They just hadn't worked the way I expected them to!
